ynthase deficiency, a type of urea cycle disorder.", "GLYCINE:Glycine is the simplest amino acid and can accumulate in the body during metabolic disturbances, contributing to neurological symptoms.", "HYPERHOMOCYSTEINEMIA:Hyperhomocysteinemia is a condition characterized by elevated levels of homocysteine in the blood, which can lead to various health issues, including cardiovascular diseases.", "CYSTEINE:", "N-ACETILGLUTAMATO SINTETASA:N-acetilglutamato sintetasa (NAGS) is an enzyme involved in the urea cycle, which helps in the metabolism of nitrogen in the body.", "CARBAMILFOSFATO SINTETASA:Carbamilfosfato sintetasa (CPS) is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the urea cycle, converting ammonia into urea.", "ORNITÍN TRANSACARBAMILASA:Ornitín transcarbamilasa (OTS) is an enzyme that catalyzes the conversion of carbamoyl phosphate and ornithine to citrulline in the urea cycle.", "ARGINOSUCCINATO SINTETASA:Arginosuccinato sintetasa (ASS) is an enzyme that facilitates the synthesis of argininosuccinate from citrulline and aspartate in the urea cycle.", "ARGINOSUCCINATO LIASA:Arginosuccinato liasa (ASL) is an enzyme that catalyzes the conversion of argininosuccinate to arginine and fumarate in the urea cycle.", "ARGINASA:Arginasa (ASA) is an enzyme that hydrolyzes arginine to ornithine and urea, playing a key role in the urea cycle.", "VITAFLO EAA:Vitaflo EAA is a dietary supplement specifically designed for the treatment of patients with urea cycle disorders, providing essential amino acids necessary for their health. It is particularly beneficial for individuals with severe metabolic disorders, including those suffering from carbamoyl phosphate synthetase (CPS) and ornithine transcarbamylase (OTC) deficiencies. This product plays a crucial role in amino acid supplementation, helping to manage the dietary needs of affected patients."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p"